The NSFNet AUP is still in force. However, it doesn't really matter, 
since nearly all commercial users have a commercial internet provider,
who has a connection to the Commercial Internet Exchange (CIX). 
The only reason you need to use NSFNet is to get to folks at government-
sponsered institutions (including most Universities).

You can always use 'traceroute' to make sure your packets are going to
stay on commercial networks.

